## Task 8: LLM summary (Gemini) with validator and template fallback (done; Gemini answer to verify on the first scheduled runs in Task 10)

**What was done**
- First check: Task 7 live run 42516537184 already verified (baseline, 0 critical, 0 warning, 3 info), marked done above.
- `src/seo_reviewer/summarize.py`:
  - `summarize(cfg, doc, env=None, session=None, sleep=...)` -> summary record; never raises for API problems. `write_summary(root, day, rec)` writes data/snapshots/DAY/summary.json; `load_summary(root, day, doc)` reads it back and falls back to the template if it is missing or belongs to an older findings.json (sha256 check).
  - Gemini call: POST llm.endpoint ({model} = llm.model), header X-goog-api-key from env llm.api_key_env, generationConfig {maxOutputTokens: llm.max_output_tokens (800), temperature 0.2, thinkingConfig {thinkingBudget: llm.thinking_budget (0)}}, timeout (10 s connect, llm.timeout_seconds read). One retry on 5xx after 2 s; 429 and timeouts are not retried. The key is never stored and is scrubbed from every error text.
  - Input to the model = compact findings.json (headline, counts, source status/error/compared_to, up to 40 findings without suggested_next_step or details, max 3 example URLs per grouped finding, ongoing counts). Prompt rules: only these findings, regressions first, reference ids, only URLs/numbers from the input, no new numbers, no next steps, plain text, max 5 lines / 100 words.
  - Validator: URLs (trailing slash ignored), numbers and finding ids must appear in the data the model got; not empty, not cut off (finishReason MAX_TOKENS), not blocked (promptFeedback.blockReason / other finishReason), <= 1500 chars. Fail -> template, reason "Gemini summary failed validation: ..." and the rejected text is kept in summary.json for debugging.
  - Template (deterministic): headline, "SOURCE failed: ERROR." lines, top 3 findings ("F001 info: message (N URLs) [evidence]"), "... and N more in the report." Used when llm.enabled is false, no key, 429/5xx/4xx, timeout, connection error, empty/blocked/cut-off answer, validation failure.
  - Record: schema_version, date, findings_generated_at, findings_sha256, generated_at, source (gemini/template), reason, model, text, finding_ids, validation_errors, rejected_text (only on validation failure), usage {prompt_tokens, output_tokens, thought_tokens, total_tokens}. Task 9 can read summary.json for the Telegram message.
- `report.py`: "## Summary" right after the header (before the baseline note / source health), with an italic line "Written by Gemini (gemini-2.5-flash) from findings.json only; checked: ..." or "Template summary (no AI). Gemini not used: REASON."; the template's first line (= headline) is not repeated. Footer says which part is AI-written. Everything else is unchanged and deterministic.
- `main.py`: default run = collect -> diff -> summarize (summary.json) -> report. The run log prints "Summary written to ...: Gemini MODEL (tokens: prompt X, output Y, thinking Z)" or "template (Gemini not used: REASON)" plus the text and any rejected-validation reasons. --collect-only and --diff-only unchanged (no Gemini call); --report-only reuses summary.json, no network, prints "summary: gemini|template".
- `diff.py`: summary.json is not read as a source record (one-line change).
- `config.py`: llm.provider must be gemini, llm.model must not contain "latest", llm.endpoint must contain {model}. `config.yaml`: only the thinking_budget comment changed.
- `.github/workflows/crawl-check.yml`: dry-run step passes GEMINI_API_KEY from secrets; step renamed "Collect + diff + summary + report dry run".
- Tests: 230 total (31 new: tests/test_summarize.py, one in test_main.py, one in test_config.py). Fake Gemini session: ok, request shape (header, maxOutputTokens 800, thinkingBudget 0, timeout), 429 (not retried), 503 then 500, 503 then ok, 400, timeout, connection error, empty, MAX_TOKENS, SAFETY, blockReason, no candidates, non-JSON, invented number, invented URL, unknown id, key scrubbing, disabled, missing/blank key, stale summary.json, report sections. conftest removes GEMINI_API_KEY from the environment for every test, so no test can call the real API. All pass on Python 3.13 in the cloud; compiled and config loads on the device's Python 3.10.

