## Task 6: diff engine and severity rules (done)

**What was done**
- `src/seo_reviewer/rules.py`: one entry per rule id (47 rules) with default severity, check label and suggested_next_step (written by the rules, never the LLM). resolved / recovered / improved / cleared findings are always info; an unconfirmed PSI lab drop ("pending") is always info. `rules.severity_overrides` in config.yaml can change a rule's severity (validated: known rule id, critical/warning/info).
- `src/seo_reviewer/diff.py`: `build_findings(cfg, root, day, records=None, compare_to=None)` -> findings document; `write_findings()` writes data/snapshots/YYYY-MM-DD/findings.json (atomic, compact); `format_findings()` for the log.
  - Source gating: failed = exactly one finding "SOURCE failed: ERROR" (robots/sitemap/crawl critical, links/psi warning), no per-URL findings; if the upstream source failed too (crawl <- robots, links <- crawl) it is an info "not run" finding. Partial = one info finding with the reasons, then a like-for-like compare. Disabled = listed, not compared. Baseline per source = `last_day_with_status(source, before=today)` (ok only), or `--compare-to`. Previous day failed + today ok = info "recovered".
  - robots: key URL allowed -> disallowed critical; mode -> disallow_all critical; parsed <-> allow_all info; declared sitemaps changed info.
  - sitemap: added URLs info (one finding with the URL list), removed info, removed > thresholds.sitemap_drop_percent (10%) warning, lastmod changed info (one finding). Partial today = added only (missing files would look like removals).
  - crawl (per page, matched by URL key): HTTP >= 400 critical, noindex critical, canonical missing critical, fetch failed / robots disallowed / redirects / canonical other / multiple canonicals / canonical target broken (from crawl + link results) / title missing / description missing / H1 missing = warning; title or description length, duplicate title or description across crawled pages, multiple H1, title/description/H1 changed = info; canonical changed = warning. Issue new on a page = change "appeared"; gone = "resolved" (info); on both days = "ongoing" (not a finding); page new in the newest-N window = "new_page". Trailing slash: see decisions.
  - links: new broken internal link warning (also "not checked" yesterday -> broken today), broken on both days = ongoing, fixed = info, newly redirecting = info. Links that are crawled pages (source crawl) are left to the crawl rules (no double report).
  - PSI lab (score, LCP, CLS, TBT; per URL x strategy): replay of the ok runs in earlier snapshots; regressed = beyond thresholds; pending info "possible regression, awaiting confirmation (k of N)", confirmed warning (then the new value is the reference, not repeated), cleared info. Failed runs/days are skipped (neither advance nor reset). CrUX compared directly with the previous ok run by category: FAST -> SLOW critical (crux_poor), other worse step warning, better info, data appearing/disappearing info; URL and origin separate, origin once per strategy. Baseline lists SLOW (warning) and AVERAGE (info) CrUX metrics.
  - More than rules.group_min (5) findings with the same source, rule and change = one grouped finding (count, items capped at rules.max_urls_per_finding). PSI is never grouped.
  - Ordering: critical, warning, info; inside a severity regressions first, then source order robots, sitemap, crawl, links, psi. Ids F001...
  - findings.json: schema_version, tool_version, date, generated_at, site, compare_to, status (baseline / issues / stable), all_stable, headline, counts, sources {status, error, compared_to, baseline, notes}, findings [{id, severity, source, rule, check, change, regression, url, old_value, new_value, evidence "old -> new", evidence_source, compared_to, message, suggested_next_step, count, details?, items?}], ongoing [{rule, severity, check, count, urls}].
- `main.py`: default mode (no flag) = collect + diff (writes findings.json, summary prints the findings). `--collect-only` unchanged. New `--diff-only` (no network, rebuild findings.json for an existing --date) and `--compare-to YYYY-MM-DD`.
- `config.py` + `config.yaml`: new `rules` section (trailing_slash_equivalent true, group_min 5, max_urls_per_finding 50, severity_overrides {}) and thresholds.sitemap_drop_percent 10.
- `.github/workflows/crawl-check.yml`: the dry-run step now runs collect + diff (`python -m seo_reviewer.main --config config.yaml`), so the log shows the real baseline findings. Nothing is committed by the workflow.
- Tests: 183 total (36 new in tests/test_diff.py, 2 new in tests/test_main.py, incl. two days of real collector records = all stable). All pass on Python 3.13 in the cloud; syntax checked on the device's Python 3.10; config.yaml loads.

