## Task 5: PageSpeed Insights collector (done)

**What was done**
- `src/seo_reviewer/collectors/psi.py`: `collect_psi(cfg, deadline, ...)`. One run per URL x strategy: psi.urls (empty = homepage; relative entries resolved against base_url; other hosts ignored with a note; duplicates removed) x psi.strategies. PSI API v5 runPagespeed, `category=performance`, key from env psi.api_key_env (PSI_API_KEY) as the `key` query parameter.
- Per run: url, strategy, status (ok / failed / skipped), error, http_status, attempts, duration_s, lighthouse_version, fetched_at, final_url, run_warnings, lab {performance_score 0-100, lcp_ms, cls, tbt_ms}, field {url, origin, notes}. field.url / field.origin = {overall_category, metrics {lcp_ms, inp_ms, cls: {percentile (p75), category FAST/AVERAGE/SLOW}}} or null. "no field data (CrUX) for this URL / for the origin" is written in field.notes. When PSI sends origin data in loadingExperience (origin_fallback), it is NOT stored as URL data. CrUX CLS percentile is divided by 100 (PSI sends x100).
- Own small client `PsiClient` (not the PoliteClient; robots.txt and the site rate limit do not apply to Google's API): read timeout psi.timeout_seconds, 10 s connect, psi.max_retries retries on 429/5xx/timeouts/connection errors (5 s backoff), no retry on 400/403. Google's error.message is kept in the error text. The key is never in the record, and every error text is scrubbed of it (`key=***`). Lighthouse runtimeError or no score = run failed, lab null.
- Record: status ok / partial / failed / disabled, error, partial_reasons, notes, endpoint, limits, strategies, urls, counts (ok, failed, skipped, no_url_field_data), requests_made, runs, collected_at. No key = failed "no API key: environment variable PSI_API_KEY is not set", no request.
- Budget: `main.collect` starts PSI in a background thread (`PsiWorker`, stdlib threading) at the start of the run, in parallel with robots/sitemap/crawl/links, same runtime.budget_seconds. A call or retry starts only if it can finish before the deadline at the full psi.timeout_seconds; otherwise it is skipped (record partial). main waits at most until the deadline + 5 s; a hang or crash becomes "PSI failed: ..." and the other sources are kept. Expected run time stays ~211 s (PSI 2 calls ~20-60 s run meanwhile).
- `main.py --collect-only` writes psi.json; summary has a psi line, "PSI failed: ..." when failed, one row per run (status | strategy | score | LCP | CLS | TBT | time | url) plus a CrUX line (URL and origin), and "requests made: N to the site, M to the PSI API".
- `config.py`: new cross-check psi.timeout_seconds < runtime.budget_seconds.
- `.github/workflows/crawl-check.yml`: the dry-run step gets `PSI_API_KEY: ${{ secrets.PSI_API_KEY }}`.
- Tests: 145 total (24 new in tests/test_psi.py, 3 new in test_main.py, 1 in test_config.py). Fixtures tests/fixtures/psi/*.json (ok with URL + origin CrUX, origin_fallback, no field data, Lighthouse runtime error, HTTP 400/403/429 bodies). All pass on Python 3.13 in the cloud; syntax checked on the device's Python 3.10.

**Files created / changed**
- New: `src/seo_reviewer/collectors/psi.py`, `tests/test_psi.py`, `tests/fixtures/psi/{mobile_ok,desktop_origin_fallback,no_field_data,runtime_error,error_400,error_403,error_429}.json`
- Changed: `src/seo_reviewer/main.py`, `src/seo_reviewer/config.py`, `tests/test_main.py`, `tests/test_config.py`, `.github/workflows/crawl-check.yml`, `DECISIONS.md` (3 entries), `STATUS.md`
- No new dependency (threading is stdlib). config.yaml unchanged.

**Decisions made** (logged in DECISIONS.md)
- Own PSI client instead of PoliteClient; key as `key` param, redacted from errors.
- PSI runs in parallel with the site collectors; "must fit the deadline at full timeout" rule; crash/hang = PSI failed.
- Record shape, origin_fallback handling, CLS /100.

**Open issues**
- RESOLVED: LIVE CHECK 3 (2026-11-08 18:43 UTC, run 42511346871, commit 2c67a54) after Hakob replaced the PSI_API_KEY secret: psi ok, 2 of 2 runs ok, 2 API requests. Homepage mobile: score 96, LCP 2701 ms, CLS 0.0, TBT 0 ms, 46.0 s; CrUX URL FAST (LCP 996 ms, INP 130 ms, CLS 0.0), origin FAST (LCP 1607 ms, INP 133 ms, CLS 0.0). Desktop: score 100, LCP 607 ms, CLS 0.0027, TBT 0 ms, 50.2 s; CrUX URL FAST (LCP 734, INP 29, CLS 0.0), origin FAST (LCP 1057, INP 34, CLS 0.0). Field names in the real response parse as expected (lab + URL and origin CrUX). PSI ran ~96 s in parallel: dry-run step 210 s, 211 site requests, inside the 300 s budget. Runs 1-2 got HTTP 403 ("...RunPagespeed are blocked" / "Permission denied on the service") because the secret held a different key.
- (history) LIVE CHECK 1 (2026-11-08 18:24 UTC, run 42509813963, commit 2c67a54): workflow green, dry-run step 211 s (PSI ran in parallel, no extra time), 211 site requests + 2 PSI requests. PSI failed as designed with HTTP 403 "Requests to this API pagespeedonline method ...RunPagespeed are blocked." on both strategies (no retry, 0.1 s). That message means the key's API restrictions do not include the PageSpeed Insights API (or the key belongs to another project). Hakob to fix the key, then re-run crawl-check. Field names still to be confirmed on a real response.
- LIVE CHECK 2 (18:36 UTC, run 42510801680): still 403, mobile "Permission denied on the service.", desktop "...RunPagespeed are blocked." Hakob's key shows API restriction = PageSpeed Insights API (set long ago). Likely the PSI_API_KEY secret holds a different key; Hakob to test the key in a browser (runPagespeed?url=https://example.com&key=...) and re-paste the secret, then re-run crawl-check.
- (Before run 1) needs the GitHub secret PSI_API_KEY (Hakob creates it, see below), then push and run crawl-check manually. A keyless call from the cloud got HTTP 429 (Google's shared keyless daily quota), so a key is required.
- How to get the key: Google Cloud console -> create/select a project -> APIs & Services -> Library -> "PageSpeed Insights API" -> Enable -> Credentials -> Create credentials -> API key -> restrict it to the PageSpeed Insights API. GitHub repo -> Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions -> New repository secret, name PSI_API_KEY. Locally: put it in .env (the code does not read .env by itself; export it or `set -a; . ./.env` before running).
- The JSON field names (finalDisplayedUrl, runtimeError, loadingExperience.origin_fallback, CrUX metric names) follow the PSI v5 docs; the first live run should be checked against a real response.
- Regression confirmation (psi.regression_confirmations, lab only; CrUX direct) is task 6.
- A daily-quota 429 is retried once (5 s, harmless).
- If psi.urls grows (each URL = 2 calls, ~20-60 s), calls are sequential inside the PSI thread; more than ~4 URLs may hit the budget (skipped, partial). Option for later: run strategies in parallel.
