## Task 4: broken link checker (done)

**What was done**
- `src/seo_reviewer/collectors/links.py`: `collect_links(client, cfg, crawl_record, deadline)`. Input = internal_links of every crawled page with status ok and seo data (HTTP 200 HTML), with the crawled pages that link to each URL (`linked_from`, first 20 stored, `linked_from_count` exact). URLs the crawl already fetched today (page URL, or the final URL of a same-host redirect) reuse the crawl result (`source: "crawl"`, no second request, not counted in the cap). The rest are ordered most-linked first, then alphabetical; the first `links.max_links` are checked (`source: "check"`), the others only counted in `left_out_by_cap`.
- Checking goes through PoliteClient (robots.txt obeyed: a disallowed link or redirect hop is recorded as disallowed and never requested; rate limit; retries). links.method HEAD first; GET (stream=True, body not read) when HEAD gets a network error or any HTTP status >= 400 (incl. 405/501), noted per link in `notes`. Redirects followed by hand (max 10, loop detection, every hop robots-checked, `redirect_chain` [{url, status, location, method}]); off-host redirects recorded, followed only if check_external. links.check_external false = same host only (the crawl stores same-host links only, so true has no extra effect yet; noted in the record).
- Per link: url, status (ok/failed/disallowed/skipped), source, http_status, final_url, redirect_chain, method, error, notes, linked_from, linked_from_count. `is_broken()` = failed or final HTTP >= 400.
- Record: status ok / partial (failed or skipped links, or crawl partial) / failed (crawl failed or missing, or no link could be checked) / disabled (links.enabled false, nothing requested); error, partial_reasons, notes (truncated pages, other-host links, cap), limits, unique_links, from_crawl, to_check, left_out_by_cap, counts (ok, failed, disallowed, skipped, broken, http_4xx, http_5xx, redirected, from_crawl, checked, get_fallback). Links listed most-linked first.
- Same runtime.budget_seconds deadline as the crawl: no new link after it; the rest are skipped and the record is partial with the reason.
- `main.py --collect-only` now writes links.json too; summary has a links line plus up to 50 rows of broken / redirected / disallowed links (status, http, method, linked-from count, url -> final).
- Tests: 120 total (18 new in tests/test_links.py; test_main.py extended). `tests/conftest.py` make_response now marks the body as read so Response.close() works on fakes. All pass on Python 3.12 and 3.13 in the cloud; syntax checked on the device's Python 3.10.

**Files created / changed**
- New: `src/seo_reviewer/collectors/links.py`, `tests/test_links.py`
- Changed: `src/seo_reviewer/main.py`, `tests/test_main.py`, `tests/conftest.py`, `config.yaml` (links.max_links 300 -> 150), `DECISIONS.md` (2 entries), `STATUS.md`
- No new dependency. crawl-check.yml unchanged: its dry-run step now also runs the link check.

**Decisions made** (logged in DECISIONS.md)
- Link checker design (reuse crawl results, ordering, HEAD -> GET fallback on any failure, status semantics, cap is not a failure).
- links.max_links 300 -> 150: at 1 req/s 300 links alone would use the whole 5-min budget after a ~1 min crawl, so links would be partial every day and PSI would have no time. Hakob confirmed (Claude recommended).

**Open issues**
- RESOLVED: live run on GitHub Actions (2026-11-08 18:05 UTC, run 42508138611, commit 80c3ed7): links ok. 1043 unique internal links on the 51 pages; 3 reused from the crawl, 150 checked with HEAD (0 needed GET), 0 broken, 0 redirected, 0 disallowed, 0 skipped; 890 left out by the cap. Whole dry-run step 211 s, 211 requests (crawl ~60 s, links ~150 s), inside the 300 s budget.
- Only 3 links matched crawled pages: posts are crawled at the sitemap form without trailing slash (/vole-mole), but pages link to the slash form (/vole-mole/). Both answer 200 with no redirect, so the site serves duplicate URLs. Task 6 should decide whether to treat a trailing-slash-only difference as the same URL (also for canonical "other", see Task 3).
- Coverage: with max_links 150 and most-linked-first order, the same ~150 site-wide links (navigation, tags, popular posts) are checked every day and ~890 article-body links never are. Stable for diffs, but a broken link inside a new post is likely missed. Option for later (task 6/10, Hakob to decide): give links from the newest pages priority, or rotate the unchecked rest across days.
- Budget sharing with PSI (task 5): crawl ~1 min + links ~2.5 min leaves ~1.5 min. Task 5 must decide order or a reserved share (PSI calls take 10-40 s each).
- check_external true needs the crawler to also store external links (not done; off by default).
- Posts link to the sitemap URL form without trailing slash vs canonical with slash (see Task 3); if links point at /x and /x/ both, they are two URLs here.
- Still open: Node 20 action versions (task 10), robotparser first-match order (task 11 docs), CRLF diffs, API keys and Telegram bot (PLAN.md §10 item 3), repo growth from crawl.json/links.json (task 10).

**Ready to commit**
Committing is entirely up to Hakob (any split is fine). Optional hint: `task 4: broken link checker (HEAD with GET fallback, robots-aware, capped)`

## Task 3: on-page crawler (done)

**What was done**
- `src/seo_reviewer/collectors/crawl.py`: `select_pages(cfg, sitemap_record)` picks homepage + `crawler.extra_urls` (absolute or relative to base_url; other hosts ignored with a note) + the newest `crawler.max_pages` sitemap URLs by lastmod (parse_lastmod; same host only; undated URLs fill up after dated ones; duplicates removed). Sitemap failed -> homepage + extra_urls only, noted; sitemap partial -> picks from what was read, noted. `collect_crawl(client, cfg, sitemap_record, deadline)` fetches each page through PoliteClient with `allow_redirects=False` and follows redirects by hand (max 10 hops, same host only, loop detection), so every hop is robots-checked, rate-limited and stored in `redirect_chain` [{url, status, location}]. Off-host redirects are recorded, not followed.
- Per page: url, reason (homepage / extra_url / sitemap), lastmod, status, error, http_status, final_url, redirect_chain, content_type, x_robots_tag (list), noindex + noindex_sources (x-robots-tag / meta-robots; "none" counts; UA-prefixed X-Robots-Tag only for googlebot), and `seo` (only for HTTP 200 HTML): title (+count, whitespace normalised, svg titles ignored), meta_description (+count; "" = present but empty, null = missing), h1 list, canonical (absolute, resolved against <base href>), canonical_raw, canonical_count, meta_robots (robots + googlebot), lang, links_total, internal_links (absolute, no fragment, deduped, max 1000/page) + internal_links_truncated. Charset from Content-Type, else bs4 detects it from the page. At most 5 MB of HTML parsed.
- Page status: ok (got a final response, any HTTP code) / failed (network error after retries, redirect loop, >10 redirects) / disallowed (robots; not fetched, also when a redirect hop is disallowed) / skipped (runtime budget). Record status: ok / partial (failed or skipped pages, or sitemap not ok) / failed (nothing fetched, e.g. robots.txt unreachable -> every page recorded as disallowed). `counts` = ok, failed, disallowed, skipped, http_200, redirected, noindex. `selection_notes` and `partial_reasons` say why.
- `http_client.py`: added `PoliteClient.now()` (the injectable clock), used for the budget deadline.
- `main.py --collect-only` now also writes crawl.json. runtime.budget_seconds counts from the start of the run; the crawl starts no new request after it. The summary prints a crawl line plus one row per page (status, http, title length, description length, H1 count, canonical self/other/missing, noindex, internal links, url), so the crawl-check workflow log shows real values.
- Tests: 100 total (17 new in tests/test_crawl.py, test_main.py updated), no network. Fixture HTML in tests/fixtures/crawl/ (home, noindex post, messy page with <base>, two descriptions, multi-valued rel canonical, three H1s; windows-1252 page). All pass on Python 3.12; syntax checked on the device's Python 3.10.

**Files created / changed**
- New: `src/seo_reviewer/collectors/crawl.py`, `tests/test_crawl.py`, `tests/fixtures/crawl/{home,post-noindex,post-messy,latin1}.html`
- Changed: `src/seo_reviewer/main.py`, `src/seo_reviewer/http_client.py` (now()), `src/seo_reviewer/config.py` (2 new keys), `config.yaml` (sitemap_include/exclude), `tests/test_main.py`, `tests/test_config.py`, `DECISIONS.md` (2 entries), `STATUS.md`
- No new dependency. crawl-check.yml unchanged: its existing dry-run step now also crawls (about 60 requests, ~1 min at 1 req/s).

**Decisions made** (logged in DECISIONS.md)
- Manual redirect following, page/record status semantics, HTTP 4xx/5xx recorded as data (status ok) for the diff to judge, internal links per page capped at 1000.

**Open issues**
- RESOLVED: live run on GitHub Actions (2026-11-08 17:36 UTC, run 42505789427, commit 3051cf6): crawl ok, 51 pages selected, 51 fetched, all HTTP 200, 0 redirected, 0 noindex, 0 failed/disallowed/skipped; 61 requests total, dry-run step took 60 s. Sitemap now ok with 10,236 URLs from all 9 files.
- DONE after the first live run: the 50 newest by lastmod were mostly tag pages (17), author pages (12) and translated pages (18); only 5 English posts (tag/author lastmods change whenever a post is published). Hakob chose to add `crawler.sitemap_include` / `crawler.sitemap_exclude` (regexes on the URL path, re.search; only for the sitemap pick, not homepage/extra_urls; validated in config.py). config.yaml excludes ^/tag/, ^/author/, ^/[a-z]{2}-[a-z]{2}/. 102 tests pass. Live re-run (2026-11-08 17:42 UTC, run 42506291195, commit 045711e): crawl ok, homepage + 50 English posts, all HTTP 200, 0 redirected/noindex/failed; 6545 sitemap URLs left out by the patterns; 61 requests, 60 s. Some old posts (e.g. 2014 Heartbleed posts) are in the newest 50 because the site bumped their lastmod. All 50 posts have canonical 'other' (sitemap URL without trailing slash vs canonical); task 6 should decide whether a trailing-slash-only difference counts.
- Observation: posts show canonical "other" (sitemap lists /vole-mole without trailing slash, no redirect; canonical most likely the slash version). Tag/author/locale pages are canonical self. Author pages have no meta description; homepage title is 15 chars. These are real data for task 6 rules.
